# A seamless 24x24 grass tile for the mossy ruins: a calm base, a few soft patches, blades and tufts
# spread evenly, a couple of lichen flowers. Every generator works on the tile as a torus (wrap=on),
# so it tiles by construction. The texture is a macro: `call grass seed=<n>` with another seed is
# a variant (examples/scripts/grass_b.pclaw and grass_c.pclaw fork this tape and do just that).
new tile grass 24x24
# Blades curve up from a dark root to a light tip; a tuft is a few of them together.
stamp save blade <<
  .d
  d.
  b.
>>
stamp save tuft <<
  d...d
  .d.d.
  .cdc.
  .bbb.
>>
def grass() {
  noise ramp=moss weights=0,3,12,1,0 cluster=1..2 density=0.07 base=moss2
  noise ramp=moss weights=0,4,10,0,0 cluster=3..6 density=0.07 base=keep
  scatter stamp=blade count=12 minDist=5 flip=on
  scatter stamp=tuft count=3 minDist=10 flip=on
  scatter c=lichen count=2 minDist=10
}
call grass seed=11
